  message: "STILL THE BLOCKER FOR THIS SPELLING AFTER WI-nisud (PR #967), and the two now\ncompose cleanly. WI-nisud made a registration edge call-shaped for taint by\npredicate (edge_types.is_callback_registration matches references +\nevidence_type=callback_argument_reference). It does nothing here because the\ndefect this item records is that NO edge exists at all: re-measured at tip on a\ntwo-arm fixture, ws.onmessage = handle emits only\n\n    calls     viaNamedAssignment -> WebSocket:0-0:onmessage:external_symbol\n    contains  file -> handle\n\nwith nothing from the registering function to handle, exactly as filed.\n\nSO THE ORDER IS: this item supplies the missing edge, WI-nisud already supplies\nthe crossing. If the edge is emitted with evidence_type\ncallback_argument_reference -- the same stamp js_ts.py already uses for the two\nsibling positions this item names, the object-literal pair branch and\n_emit_anon_callback_reference_edges -- then taint picks it up with no further\nchange, and the named-assignment spelling starts producing findings the day the\nedge lands. Worth pinning that in whatever test ships with it, because the\ncoupling is invisible from this side.\n\nNOT A PRIORITY ARGUMENT. Raising P3 is the owner's call; this is only the\ndependency note."  # d1df
